      "file": "src/Caching/ProductCacheDecorator.cs",
      "line": 14,
      "description": "**Role:** Sits in front of ProductRepository; returns the cached value on a hit, otherwise reads through and caches the result.\n**Risk:** new caching layer, correctness-sensitive\n\n**Look for:** cache entries have no expiration — eviction relies entirely on CacheInvalidationHandler firing.\n\n**Discussion:** if an invalidation event is ever missed, does anything else bound how stale a cached entry can get? (🟡 Significant)"
    }
